%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Run Javascript

Here is an example of how to trigger confetti with an external JavaScript library. To understand how Wolfram Language integrates with JavaScript, check out these guides:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/party-js@latest/bundle/party.min.js"></script>

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: html
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/party-js@latest/bundle/party.min.js"></script>

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Now it is in the global Javascript scope. Define a javascript function to trigger confetti:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Now it is in the global Javascript scope. Define a javascript function to trigger confetti:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.js
core.RunFireworks = async (args, env) => {
const id = await interpretate(args[0], env);
party.confetti(document.getElementById(id).parentNode, {
  count: party.variation.range(20, 40),
  size: party.variation.range(0.8, 2.2),
});
}

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: js
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
core.RunFireworks = async (args, env) => {
const id = await interpretate(args[0], env);
party.confetti(document.getElementById(id).parentNode, {
  count: party.variation.range(20, 40),
  size: party.variation.range(0.8, 2.2),
});
}

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Here `RunFireworks[id]` accepts one argument: the ID of a DOM element whose parent will receive the confetti fireworks. We can create a dummy DOM element within a WLX component and trigger `RunFireworks` using `FrontSubmit` in response to slide events:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Here `RunFireworks[id]` accepts one argument: the ID of a DOM element whose parent will receive the confetti fireworks. We can create a dummy DOM element within a WLX component and trigger `RunFireworks` using `FrontSubmit` in response to slide events:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.wlx
Party := Module[{
  UId = CreateUUID[],
  Ev = CreateUUID[]
},
  EventHandler[Ev, {
      "Slide" -> Function[Null,
          FrontSubmit[RunFireworks[UId]]
      ]
  }];
  <div id="{UId}">
      <SlideEventListener Id={Ev}/>
  </div>
]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Now if you place it on any slide, it will launch confetti once the slide has become visible. For example:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Now if you place it on any slide, it will launch confetti once the slide has become visible. For example:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.slide

# Let's have

