## Programmatic slides control
Use `FrontSlidesSelected` to control slides programmatically. Note that this is a frontend function (i.e., undefined on the Wolfram Kernel). Execute it with `FrontSubmit` to navigate to a different slide programmatically. For example:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Programmatic slides control
Use `FrontSlidesSelected` to control slides programmatically. Note that this is a frontend function (i.e., undefined on the Wolfram Kernel). Execute it with `FrontSubmit` to navigate to a different slide programmatically. For example:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
FrontSlidesSelected["navigateNext", 1] // FrontSubmit

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
This will navigate the first visible presentation to the next slide. You can connect external devices and manipulate slides remotely via Wolfram Language, timers, or buttons:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
This will navigate the first visible presentation to the next slide. You can connect external devices and manipulate slides remotely via Wolfram Language, timers, or buttons:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
NavButton := Button["→", FrontSlidesSelected["navigateNext", 1] // FrontSubmit];

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Then use it on a slide:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Then use it on a slide:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.slide

Current slide

<NavButton/>

---

Next slide

